From c055f30baf92c6a18479966f5bd543e33970aac0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yumi-Lab <nicolas@yumi-lab.com>
Date: Mon, 20 Jul 2026 17:42:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 10/16] tcg: add an execution-weighted TB profile
 (QEMU_TB_EXEC_PROFILE)

Complement the static opcode histogram with a profile weighted by real
execution.  Each translated TB gets a record (guest pc, insn count, the
op list after optimization) and a 64-bit execution counter that a short
host stub emitted by tcg_out_tb_start bumps on every entry, so chained
goto_tb entries, goto_ptr lookups and main-loop entries are all counted.
Cheap counters on the dispatch paths (lookup helper calls, jump cache
hit/miss, main-loop lookups) complete the picture.  On exit the dump
reports the entry-path split, the execution-weighted opcode mix and the
hottest TBs.

The persistent translation cache is disabled while profiling: profiled
code embeds the absolute address of its counter, which is only valid in
the run that emitted it.

Overhead measured on the pad: about 17 percent on the torn64 benchmark,
zero when the profile is not enabled.
